# .claude/ is COMMITTED repo policy, not per-developer config: settings, hooks, reviewer agents,
# commands, and the skills themselves are inherited on clone. Skills are VENDORED there as real
# copied files (init-greenfield.mjs --vendor-skills), so every teammate gets the exact standard
# this repo was migrated to. `npx skills add` instead creates .claude/skills as a SYMLINK into
# ~/.agents/skills — that is the shape of a personal install, and git stores a symlink as its
# target path, so committing it would hand teammates a broken link to a path on one machine.
# Deliberately not what a repo commits, which is why .claude/skills is absent below.
#
# Ignore only what is genuinely personal, plus the home-side artifacts `npx skills add` drops here.
# No trailing slashes: those artifacts can be symlinks, and a `dir/` pattern matches only a real
# directory — so `.agents/` silently fails to ignore a symlinked `.agents` and the link gets
# committed.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/*.local.*
.agents
skills-lock.json

# Test-run output. `npm run test:coverage` and `playwright test` write these on every run, and oxfmt
# HONOURS .gitignore — measured: a gitignored `dist/` is never visited, while a tracked
# `coverage/coverage-summary.json` is, so an unignored coverage report makes `format:check` fail on a
# machine-generated file. `coverage/` also feeds the vitest.config.ts ratchet and must never be
# committed: a stale report in the tree is a floor nobody measured.
coverage
test-results
playwright-report
blob-report
playwright/.cache

# The JSON report .github/workflows/ci.yml's lint step writes into the working tree. On a runner the
# format:check step runs before it, so CI never sees it; a local run of the same steps in order does,
# and `format:check` then fails on a generated file.
oxlint-report.json

# Editor state is personal — EXCEPT the two files that defend the formatter. extensions.json
# recommends oxc and marks the Prettier extensions unwanted for this workspace; settings.json routes
# ts/tsx saves to oxfmt with per-language blocks. Without them, a save under a personal Prettier
# default emits double quotes at printWidth 80 and fails `npm run format:check` on every file.
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/settings.json
